 ('A polynomial is a sum of constant multiples of nonnegative whole-number powers of x. The largest power with a nonzero coefficient is its degree. At large positive or negative inputs, the leading term controls end behavior.', 'p(x)=(x+2)(x-1)^2'),
 ('A factored expression makes zeros visible. This function is zero at negative two and at one. The factor at negative two appears once, while the factor at one appears twice.', 'x=-2 quad x=1'),
 ('Near a zero, an odd multiplicity usually looks like crossing the axis: the sign changes. An even multiplicity touches the axis and returns to the same side. Here the double factor makes the graph bounce at one.', '"odd: cross" quad "even: touch"'),
