 ('Multiplying equal-base powers adds their exponents. That is why the logarithm of a product becomes a sum of logarithms. The quotient rule subtracts, and a power becomes a multiplier. These rules require positive arguments in the real setting.', 'log_b(x y)=log_b x+log_b y'),
